{"seconds": 66.9, "exit": 0, "final": "Again! The bishop on e6 is undefended (the king moved from f5 to e4). So White plays Kxe6 and wins the bishop in all three responses to g4+.\n\nThe brilliant point: **g4+ is a deflection move that forces the Black king away from defending the bishop on e6. In all three responses (Kxg4, Kg6, Ke4), the bishop becomes undefended and White captures it with Kxe6, winning a piece.**\n\n**Best move: g4+**\n\n**Main line:** g4+ Kg6 (or Kxg4) Kxe6, and White is up a bishop.\n\n**Motif:** deflection (the check forces the king away from defending the bishop)\n\n**Coaching explanation:** The key insight is spotting that the Black bishop on e6 is the sole defender of the rook, AND the Black king currently defends that bishop. A check that forces the king away removes that defense instantly. g4+ is a deflection: the pawn check pulls the king from f5, leaving e6 undefended. On any king move, White captures the bishop with Kxe6, winning a full piece. Look for checks that accomplish a tactical purpose\u2014here it dismantles Black's defense.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"g4+\", \"line\": [\"g4+\", \"Kg6\", \"Kxe6\"], \"motifs\": [\"deflection\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2r5/p1P5/3Kb3/4Bkp1/1P6/6P1/8/8 w - - 4 60"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2r5/p1P5/3Kb3/4Bkp1/1P6/6P1/8/8 w - - 4 60"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "2r5/p1P5/3Kb3/4Bkp1/1P6/6P1/8/8 w - - 4 60"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "2r5/p1P5/3Kb3/4Bkp1/1P6/6P1/8/8 w - - 4 60", "square": "c8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "2r5/p1P5/3Kb3/4Bkp1/1P6/6P1/8/8 w - - 4 60", "square": "c7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2r5/p1P5/3Kb3/4Bkp1/1P6/6P1/8/8 w - - 4 60", "square": "d6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2r5/p1P5/3Kb3/4Bkp1/1P6/6P1/8/8 w - - 4 60", "move": "g4"}},